From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Juho=20L=C3=A4=C3=A4kk=C3=B6?= <juho.laakko@qt.io>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 09:45:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] skcms: do not use musttail on 32-bit ARM with GCC

skcms has two exec_stages() implementations. The musttail one is marked
SI, i.e. static inline __attribute__((always_inline)); the other is a
plain static function. SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL selects between them.

The clang branch of that selection deliberately excludes 32-bit ARM,
because [[clang::musttail]] is known to break there (see the comment
above it, crbug.com/1504548). The GCC branch was added later and only
checks for the attribute, with no architecture exclusions at all. Once
GCC advertises __has_cpp_attribute(clang::musttail) - GCC 16 does - an
armv7 build therefore takes a code path upstream already knows does not
work on 32-bit ARM, and the always_inline then cannot be honoured:

  Transform_inl.h:1508:13: error: inlining failed in call to
      'always_inline' 'void skcms_private::baseline::exec_stages(...)':
      target specific option mismatch

Apply the same exclusion clang uses. Upstream has been extending this
branch one architecture at a time - riscv was added for the same class
of failure, citing gcc.gnu.org/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=121784 - so
32-bit ARM simply has not been reported yet.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/skcms_internals.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/skcms_internals.h b/chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/skcms_internals.h
index c869cd95a4bb..822755576831 100644
--- a/chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/skcms_internals.h
+++ b/chromium/third_party/skia/modules/skcms/src/skcms_internals.h
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@
             #define SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL 1
         #endif
     #elif !defined(__clang__) && !defined(SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL)
-        #if __has_cpp_attribute(clang::musttail)
+        #if __has_cpp_attribute(clang::musttail) && !defined(__arm__)
             #define SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL 1
         #else
             #define SKCMS_HAS_MUSTTAIL 0
